1
00:00:02,199 --> 00:00:05,050
Lesson 5. Ted goes out for the evening.

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,429
Ted leaves to go visit his girlfriend, Amber.

3
00:00:09,179 --> 00:00:12,189
Ted's mother, Susan, says she doesn't really like Amber.

4
00:00:12,560 --> 00:00:14,550
She wishes him a good time anyway.

5
00:00:15,380 --> 00:00:16,429
See you later, mom.

6
00:00:16,780 --> 00:00:17,929
Where are you going, Ted?

7
00:00:18,260 --> 00:00:19,669
I told Amber I'd drop by.

8
00:00:20,019 --> 00:00:21,449
What are you two going to do?

9
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:24,250
Maybe go to the movies or to a party.

10
00:00:24,359 --> 00:00:25,629
Our plans are still up in the air.

11
00:00:26,120 --> 00:00:27,769
Why don't you invite her over here?

12
00:00:28,320 --> 00:00:29,889
I don't want to hang around here.

13
00:00:30,179 --> 00:00:31,889
Dad is really down in the dumps.

14
00:00:31,980 --> 00:00:35,089
Is Amber the girl with the nose ring and the purple hair?

15
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:36,890
Yeah, I'm crazy about her.

16
00:00:37,159 --> 00:00:41,530
Don't take this the wrong way, but she's not exactly my cup of tea.

17
00:00:41,840 --> 00:00:42,769
Take it easy, mom.

18
00:00:43,200 --> 00:00:44,429
We're not about to get married.

19
00:00:44,899 --> 00:00:46,689
We just enjoy hanging out together.

20
00:00:47,420 --> 00:00:49,229
I guess there's no accounting for taste.

21
00:00:49,539 --> 00:00:50,390
Have a good time.

22
00:00:50,700 --> 00:00:52,210
Don't worry. We'll have a blast.

23
00:00:52,539 --> 00:00:53,869
That's what I'm afraid of.

